npegged is derivative work of Pegged by Philippe Sigaud and contributors,
including the Extended Pascal example contributed by its original authors.
The original sources and their attribution remain in third-party/Pegged.
Pegged's README specifies the Boost Software License 1.0, reproduced in LICENSE.

The conversion changes storage, ownership, code generation, error handling,
testing, and tooling. Existing grammar text and example expectations retain
their upstream provenance. New code is distributed under the same license.

Unicode case-fold and alphabetic-property mappings are generated from the
vendored Unicode 17.0.0 Character Database. Its copyright and Unicode License
V3 are preserved in third-party/unicode. No Phobos code or tables are linked.
